⚠️ Notice: Audit Deprecated

This audit category has been deprecated and is expected to be removed in future Windows 10 updates. However, systems should still be configured accordingly if the option is available to maintain legacy compliance until officially retired.

🔍 Finding

Auditing MPSSVC Rule-Level Policy Changes helps track changes to rules that affect the Microsoft Protection Service (MPSSVC.exe). This can be useful for detecting unauthorized or unintended modifications to system firewall policies and other rule-based configurations.

🛠️ Manual Configuration

Open Local Group Policy Editor:
Press Win + R, type gpedit.msc, and press Enter
Navigate to:

Computer Configuration >>
Windows Settings >>
Security Settings >>
Advanced Audit Policy Configuration >>
System Audit Policies >>
Policy Change
Locate and double-click:
Audit MPSSVC Rule-Level Policy Change


Check the box for:
Success
Click Apply and then OK

✅ Verification (PowerShell)

To verify this audit policy via PowerShell:

AuditPol /get /subcategory:"MPSSVC Rule-Level Policy Change"
Expected output:

MPSSVC Rule-Level Policy Change   Success
📌 Notes

Logs related to this audit appear in the Security event log.
Event IDs in this category may not appear on newer systems due to deprecation.
Keep this policy configured for legacy support where applicable.
